---
title: "Sale Lifecycle (LegionPreLiquidApprovedSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_initialized: initialize(params)
    q_initialized --> q_active: sale is active (accepting investments)
    q_active --> q_active: invest(amount, sig) [repeated]
    q_active --> q_active: refund() [during refund period]
    q_active --> q_canceled: cancel() [project, before tokens supplied]
    q_active --> q_ended: end() [Legion or project]
    q_ended --> q_refund_period: refund period active (refundEndTime)
    q_refund_period --> q_refund_period: refund() [investors can still refund]
    q_refund_period --> q_post_refund: block.timestamp >= refundEndTime
    q_post_refund --> q_capital_published: publishRaisedCapital(amount) [Legion]
    q_capital_published --> q_capital_withdrawn: withdrawRaisedCapital() [project]
    q_capital_published --> q_tge_published: publishTgeDetails(token, supply, allocated) [Legion]
    q_tge_published --> q_tokens_supplied: supplyTokens(amount, fees) [project]
    q_tokens_supplied --> q_claiming: claimTokenAllocation() [investors]
    q_claiming --> q_claiming: releaseVestedTokens() [investors]
    q_canceled --> q_investor_withdraw: withdrawInvestedCapitalIfCanceled() [investors]
    q_investor_withdraw --> [*]: all capital returned
    q_claiming --> [*]: all tokens distributed

    note right of q_active
        INV-001: investments only during active sale (not ended, not canceled)
        INV-002: refunds allowed until refundEndTime
    end note

    note right of q_post_refund
        INV-003: capital raised published by Legion after refund period
        INV-004: project withdraws capital, then Legion publishes TGE details
        INV-005: tokens supplied must equal totalTokensAllocated
    end note

    note right of q_canceled
        INV-006: cancel only before tokens supplied
        INV-007: if capital withdrawn, project must return it on cancel
        INV-008: canceled sale allows all investors to withdraw
    end note
